<title>FRANCE: EU clears duty free wheat import from Canada.</title>
<headline>EU clears duty free wheat import from Canada.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday cleared the way for the import this year of 300,000 tonnes of wheat at a zero import tariff, expected to come from Canada, grain industry sources said.</p>
<p>The decision adopted at a grain meeting in Brussels in theory applies to wheat from any origin, but is intended as a concession to Canada following recent trade negotiations, they said.</p>
<p>Further details of the imports would be known when the Commission in Brussels publishes its decision in several days time, they said.</p>
</text>
